# Generated by `expo prebuild`, here or on the EAS builder, and never
# committed: this app uses Continuous Native Generation.
#
# Listed in this directory rather than only at the repository root because
# the root .gitignore is not part of the EAS upload (see ../.easignore). The
# fingerprint that becomes the runtime version treats any native directory git
# does not ignore as hand-maintained source, so without this file the builder,
# which has just generated ios/, computes a different runtime version from the
# machine that started the build and fails it.
/ios
/android

# `eas update` exports here before uploading, and leaves it behind — 101 MB of
# bundles and source maps after one publish. Untracked it would be committed by
# a stray `git add -A`; un-ignored by .easignore it rode along in the next
# build's archive, which is how a 5 MB upload became 24 MB.
/dist
